{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-296",
  "title": "Functions as Facts",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "reviewing",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Functions as Facts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Treating **functions as facts** opens the door to using **Prolog (or a Prolog-like logic engine)** as the orchestration layer: a local reasoning substrate that’s compact, explainable, and symbolic. This positions your agent as a hybrid of *latent priors (via embeddings)* and *structured inference (via logic)*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let’s walk through why this is a powerful approach—and how to make it work."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🧩 Functions as Facts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In logic terms, a function can be represented as a **predicate with inputs and outputs**, plus possibly metadata (cost, category, state effects). For example:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```prolog"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "function(average, [List], Result) :- is_list(List), sum(List, S), length(List, L), Result is S / L."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Or abstractly:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```prolog"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "function(name(average), input_type(list), output_type(number), category(statistical), cost(low))."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now a query like:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```prolog"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "?- function(Name, input_type(list), output_type(number), category(statistical))."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Returns all functions that match the criteria—this becomes your **retrieval mechanism**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🧠 Embeddings + Prolog: A Hybrid Strategy"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-21",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Embeddings** are used to translate user queries into structured symbolic forms: e.g., extract `category`, `input_type`, or infer function names."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-22",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Prolog** then uses these as constraints to retrieve, compose, or reason about function calls."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This gives you:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-25",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Fuzzy front-end** (handle messy natural language)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-26",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Crisp back-end** (handle precise function matching and sequencing)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This mimics how a small brain might compensate for limited intuition with meticulous logic—exactly the sort of balance local-first AI needs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "✨ Why Prolog Works Well Here"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Small and fast**: Prolog interpreters can run in-browser (`tau-prolog`, `jsprolog`) and are lightweight."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Symbolic clarity**: You get transparent, explainable control over function selection."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Composability**: You can represent multi-step workflows as goal satisfaction chains."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **Extensibility**: You can model temporal state, constraints, effects, or user preferences."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🔧 Implementation Idea"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Define your function corpus** in Prolog facts."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Embed user input** using a tiny transformer or even keyword matcher."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Translate embeddings into constraints** (e.g., `wants(filter), input_type(list)`)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **Query Prolog** to get candidate functions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. **Execute or plan** using JavaScript or call stack."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Optionally:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-43",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Add weights or ranks based on embedding distance or usage frequency."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-44",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Compose multi-function plans as Prolog rules."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-47",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🪞Philosophically Speaking"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Using Prolog centers the system not on black-box cognition, but on **interpretable relationships**. It embodies a different paradigm of intelligence: not raw power, but **coherence and clarity**. This aligns beautifully with the ethos of a local-first agent—where **understanding, not just outcome**, is the goal."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🌐 Core Architecture: Hybrid Local Agent"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-51",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Functions as Logic Facts**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-52",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```prolog"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-53",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "function(avg, [list(number)], number)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "category(avg, statistical)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-55",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "alias(avg, \"average\")."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-57",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Embeddings as Fuzzy Entry Points**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-58",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Embed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-62",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-59",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "User queries"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-60",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Function docstrings"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-61",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Conceptual anchors (e.g., \"filter\", \"compare\", \"lookup\")"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Then use nearest-neighbor search to retrieve:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-67",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-64",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Function *names* (to suggest to Prolog)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-65",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "*Semantic classes* (to constrain the Prolog query)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-66",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "*Entity mentions* (to guide argument construction)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-68",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Knowledge Graph as Context Frame**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-69",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A local, compact knowledge graph (~hundreds of nodes):"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-73",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-70",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Encodes relationships between domains (e.g., `temperature -> unit -> Celsius`)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-71",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Provides auxiliary data to validate or enrich function arguments"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-72",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Acts as a *contextual substrate* for Prolog or fallback for missing knowledge"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-74",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **Planner / Orchestrator**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-78",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-75",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Embedding matches intent → translates to Prolog goals"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-76",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Prolog returns matching function(s) or plans"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-77",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "JS engine executes, logs, and feeds results back to the reasoning loop"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-79",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-80",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🛠️ Skeleton Workflow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-81",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "📥 1. User Input"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-82",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-83",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const input = \"get the average temperature for this week\";"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-84",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-85",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🔎 2. Embedding Phase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-88",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-86",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Use MiniLM to embed input"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-87",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Nearest-neighbor search returns:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-89",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- `intent`: \"average\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-90",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- `domain`: \"temperature\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-91",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- `entity`: \"week\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-93",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-92",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Translates into Prolog constraints:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-94",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```prolog"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-95",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "intent(avg)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-96",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "domain(temperature)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-97",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "time_scope(week)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-98",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-99",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🧠 3. Prolog Reasoning"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-100",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```prolog"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-101",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "function(avg_temp, [list(day_temp)], number)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-102",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "alias(avg_temp, \"average temperature\")."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-103",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "contextual_scope(avg_temp, time, week)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-104",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "entity_type(avg_temp, temperature)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-105",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "% If multiple functions match, rank via embedding distance or past usage"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-106",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-107",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Query:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-108",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```prolog"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-109",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "?- function(Fn, Args, Out), domain(Fn, temperature), time_scope(Fn, week)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-110",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-111",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "⚙️ 4. JS Function Calling"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-112",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-113",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const fn = resolveFunction(\"avg_temp\");"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-114",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "const result = fn([72, 75, 68, 70, 74, 69, 71]); // weekly temps"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-115",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-116",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🔁 5. Feedback Loop"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-120",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-117",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Result is saved"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-118",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Context graph is updated"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-119",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Function usage patterns are refined (e.g., via Hebbian heuristics)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-121",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-122",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🧬 Small-World Graph Layer"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-127",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-123",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Acts like **episodic memory**"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-124",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Connects entities (e.g., \"week\" → \"days\" → \"temperature sensors\")"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-125",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Represents evolving state"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-126",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Enables *Prolog-backed inference + vector-backed generalization*"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-128",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Useful for:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-132",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-129",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Inferring missing arguments"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-130",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Navigating from abstract prompts to concrete data"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-131",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Giving \"world awareness\" to function invocations"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-133",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-134",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🔮 Philosophical Note"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-135",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is not just computation—it's a sketch of **cognitive minimalism**. You're building an architecture that *thinks locally, reasons transparently, and remembers personally*. It resists scale fetishism in favor of coherence, intimacy, and introspection. A *slow AI*, but not a dumb one."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-136",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
